# Multi-language (i18n)

The app supports **English (`en`)** and **Vietnamese (`vi`)** via `I18nContext` (`contexts/I18nContext.tsx`). Locale is stored in `localStorage` (`aichat.locale`) and switched from **AppUserMenu**.

**Do not** hardcode user-visible UI strings in components or pages. **Do not** mix EN and VI in the same screen.

## Message files

- `apps/frontend/messages/en.json` — English (source of truth for keys)
- `apps/frontend/messages/vi.json` — Vietnamese (must mirror `en.json` key structure)

Add keys to **both** files in the same commit. Use nested namespaces:

| Namespace | Use for |
|-----------|---------|
| `nav.*` | Sidebar navigation |
| `layout.*` | App shell, user menu, mobile chrome |
| `chat.*` | Chat page, input, options menu |
| `auth.*` | Login / register |
| `settings.*` | Settings tabs and sections |
| `agents.*` | Agents pages and forms |
| `flows.*` | Flow list, designer, modals |
| `common.*` | Shared actions (save, cancel, delete…) |
| `errors.*` | Generic error fallbacks |

## Usage in components

```tsx
import { useI18n } from "@/contexts/I18nContext";

export function MyComponent() {
  const { t } = useI18n();

  return (
    <>
      <h1>{t("agents.title")}</h1>
      <p>{t("flows.deleteConfirmBody", "Flow {name} will be deleted.", { name: flowName })}</p>
    </>
  );
}
```

### Rules

1. **Every user-visible string** (labels, placeholders, `title`, `aria-label`, empty states, buttons, toasts, confirm dialogs) must use `t(key, fallback)`.
2. **Fallback** (`defaultValue`) is required when adding new keys — aids dev before JSON is complete.
3. **Interpolation**: use `{var}` in JSON and pass `vars` as third argument to `t()`.
4. **Page headers**: `PageHeader title={t("settings.title")}` — never pass raw English/Vietnamese literals.
5. **Dynamic lists**: use `labelKey` in config arrays, resolve with `t(labelKey)` at render time.
6. **`locale` prop**: only when formatting dates/numbers; UI text still goes through `t()`.
7. **Backend error messages**: may stay as returned from API; wrap only UI chrome around them.

## Provider setup

`I18nProvider` wraps the app in `app/layout.tsx`. All client pages/components under it can call `useI18n()`.

`document.documentElement.lang` is synced automatically when locale changes.

## Adding a new feature — checklist

- [ ] Identified all user-visible strings in the new UI
- [ ] Added keys to `en.json` and `vi.json` (same structure)
- [ ] Component/page uses `useI18n()` and `t()` — no hardcoded EN/VI
- [ ] `title` / `aria-label` / `placeholder` translated
- [ ] Tested with locale **EN** and **VI** (AppUserMenu → Ngôn ngữ)
- [ ] Empty states and error fallbacks translated

## Known gaps (migrate when touching a file)

These areas may still contain hardcoded strings — **wire i18n when you edit them**:

- Flow Designer (`FlowEditor.tsx`, node palette, status labels)
- Settings detail sections (persona editor, API keys UI, `ProviderModelsSection`)
- Agent forms/cards (`AgentForm`, `SystemAgentForm`, `CategoryManager`)
- System agents pages (`agents/system/*`)
- Chat message actions (`MessageBubble`, `ActionButtons`)

When migrating a file, convert **all** strings in that file in one pass, not piecemeal.

## Anti-patterns

```tsx
// ❌ Hardcoded
<button>Lưu flow</button>

// ❌ Mixed locale
<h1>Settings</h1>
<p>Cài đặt được lưu cục bộ</p>

// ❌ Locale branching for labels
{locale === "vi" ? "Hủy" : "Cancel"}

// ✅ Correct
<button>{t("common.save")}</button>
```
